type(scope): subject

Why this change is needed. The diff shows what changed; say why.

Refs #
# Format: type(scope): subject   (Conventional Commits, checked by "pnpm check:commit")
#
#   type   feat | fix | docs | refactor | chore | ci | build | test | perf
#   scope  your team label: team-1..4, platform or team-instructor
#   subject  imperative mood, lowercase, at most 72 characters, no trailing period
#            ("add login page", not "Added login page.")
#
# The body needs "Refs #<issue>" (or "Closes #<issue>") on its own line.
# Not sure about the type? Run: pnpm workflow:classify --kind commit --staged
# Lines starting with "#" are removed when you save.
